                <li><strong>Half-day compatibility:</strong> You can depart at 07:00 AM, finish your visit by 11:30 AM, and be back in District 1 for lunch.</li>
                <li><strong>Afternoon freedom:</strong> Leaves your second half of the day open for a <a href="/saigon-hop-on-hop-off-bus-guide" class="text-amber-800 hover:text-amber-900 font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 decoration-amber-300">Saigon hop-on hop-off bus</a> tour or exploring the <a href="/independence-palace-saigon-guide" class="text-amber-800 hover:text-amber-900 font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 decoration-amber-300">Independence Palace</a>.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>
                Ben Dinh is ideal for:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
                <li>First-time visitors with limited days in Ho Chi Minh City.</li>
                <li>Travelers booking a standard half-day morning tour.</li>
                <li>Families with young children or elderly relatives who tire quickly in tropical heat.</li>
                <li>Visitors planning a balanced <a href="/cu-chi-tunnels-half-day-vs-full-day" class="text-amber-800 hover:text-amber-900 font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 decoration-amber-300">half-day vs. full-day Cu Chi tour comparison</a>.</li>
