              </h2>
            </div>

            <div class="text-slate-700 text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed space-y-4">
              <p>
                Misconceptions about tunnel crawl dimensions are widespread online:
              </p>
              <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-600 text-sm">
                <li>At <strong>Ben Duoc</strong>, the main visitor corridors average <strong>62 to 75 cm in width</strong> and <strong>95 to 104 cm in height</strong>.</li>
                <li>At <strong>Ben Dinh</strong>, the primary levels measure roughly <strong>62 to 65 cm wide</strong> and <strong>105 to 110 cm high</strong>, with certain constricted passages dipping to <strong>40 cm by 73 cm</strong>.</li>
              </ul>
              <p>
                While select sections have been enlarged for international tourism, the physical experience remains restrictive. You will duck-walk or crawl on hands and knees through humid, red-clay passages. Wearing loose, breathable clothes and packing a <a href="/khan-ran-nam-bo" class="text-amber-800 hover:text-amber-900 font-semibold underline underline-offset-2 decoration-amber-300">traditional khăn rằn checkered scarf</a> to wipe away sweat will make your on-site exploration far more comfortable.
              </p>
