                A standard half-day excursion is designed to provide an introduction to the tunnels and return you to Ho Chi Minh City without consuming your entire daylight window.
              </p>
              <p>
                An independent visit can be far more flexible. The wider visitor areas contain historical displays, reconstructed spaces, models, artefacts, and commemorative areas beyond the tunnel passages themselves.
              </p>
              <p>
                This is particularly relevant at Ben Duoc: a traveler interested in the broader history, memorial complex, and preserved landscape can comfortably spend 3 to 4 unhurried hours exploring the grounds.
